# Example user crontab entry for ubuntu-health-check.
# Runs unprivileged on the 1st day of each month at 10:00.
#
# Install it from the tool directory (replaces @UHC_DIR@ with the real path
# and appends the line to your existing crontab):
#   (crontab -l 2>/dev/null; grep -v '^#' contrib/crontab.example | sed "s|@UHC_DIR@|$PWD|") | crontab -
#
# The tool sets its own PATH and finds your desktop session for notifications.
#
# m  h  dom mon dow  command
0 10 1 * * "@UHC_DIR@/uhc.sh" --quiet
